ADR-0017
title: Public turn clock with three intra-turn beats
status: Accepted
date: 2026-08-16
decision_owner: Product owner
related:
  - ADR-0001
  - ADR-0006
  - ADR-0016
  - docs/battle-pacing-candidate-12-v2.md
authority: this file is the causal record; 0017-public-turn-intra-turn-beats.md is the projection

PROBLEM P1
  ADR-0016 grouped K=3 engine resolutions for narration but counted
  each resolution as a public ターン. The owner never accepted
  beat = turn. The 12-turn pacing clock and the intra-turn
  subdivision were collapsed into one counter.

EVIDENCE E1
  candidate-12-v2 freezes turnLimit 12 as the public match clock.
EVIDENCE E2
  Production UI and 物語 headings printed engine resolution
  numbers as ターン N.
EVIDENCE E3
  Owner 2026-08-16: beat is not a turn; reconstitute as twelve
  turns with three beats each; do not show turns to the narrator.

CAUSE C1
  Implementation treated the existing engine turn increment as the
  micro-turn identity. That made K consume the public clock.

REJECTED O1: keep 0016 clock and only hide headings
  Display lie. Pacing, turn-limit, and story identity stay wrong.
REJECTED O2: raise turnLimit to 36 and keep one counter
  Still names beats as turns.

DECISION O3: public turn is the 12-count clock. Each public
  combat turn contains up to K=3 sequential engine beats.
  Narration still fires on beat-group close. Public 物語 and
  narrator-facing copy do not display turn numbers. The match
  header may show ターン N / 12.

OWNER_ACCEPTANCE
  Product owner directed this reconstitution on 2026-08-16:
  do not equate beat with turn; no narrator turn display;
  twelve turns, three beats per turn.

ACCEPTANCE
  ADR-0017 revision dated 2026-08-16 is Accepted. Selected
  option is O3. This amends ADR-0016 R1/R3 clock identity.
  ADR-0016 skip-LLM, reserved actions, and sequential order remain.

RULES
  R1. New battles bind sceneBeat.clock = public-turn. Missing
      clock keeps ADR-0016 micro-turn increment for in-flight
      battles.
  R2. Public state.turn increments only when a new public combat
      turn starts. Continuing beats keep the same turn.
  R3. K=3 beats belong inside one public turn. Close still uses
      K, 15% HP swing, KO/terminal, or infeasible reservation.
  R4. turnLimit 12 counts public turns. Turn-limit finish waits
      until the last beat of public turn 12, unless KO ends first.
  R5. combatTick increments every engine beat. Causal execution
      identity includes beat index so two beats of one turn do
      not resume each other.
  R6. Restoration, due-turn effects, happenings, and battlefield
      intro run on the first beat of a public turn only.
  R7. Public 物語 headings and narrator-facing presentation do
      not print ターン numbers. Header ターン N / 12 remains.
  R8. Auto-advance HTTP remains one beat per call.
  R9. No database migration.

CONSEQUENCES
  + Public clock matches the 12-turn pacing policy.
  + Three engine exchanges can land in one public turn / one story.
  + In-flight 0016 battles keep their recorded increment.
  - A public turn can take three HTTP advances before the header
    increments; beat index is shown beside the header.
  - Matches last up to 36 combat beats.

COMPATIBILITY
  Battles without sceneBeat.clock keep 0016 counting.
  New battles created after this ADR use public-turn.
